    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d142-a3">

                <pb facs="0378" n="294" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg294"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Kelly to Mr. Flores.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Victoria Hotel</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-06-27"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 27,
                        1886</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Flores</hi>: In reply to the three
                    questions foregoing, I beg to say to the first that I am an English subject; to
                    the second, that when I left Ecuador recently, like everybody else I had to
                    provide myself with a passport from the governor of Guayaquil, without which the
                    steamship company would not have sold me tickets; and to the third, that I have
                    never considered my English nationality in any way endangered or made
                    questionable by having an Ecuadorian passport in my possession.</p>
                <p>Yours, very truly,</p>
                <closer><signed>M. J. KELLY.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
